/* Tanker Rent UK Ltd Master Hire Agreement – transcribed from the signed PDF (27/11/2026). Check against the original before relying on it. */
window.CT_TERMS = {"title": "Master hire agreement", "blocks": [{"h": "Definitions"}, {"p": "“Collection Date” shall mean the date on which the Hirer shall take physical possession of the Trailer from the Company, as specified in the Trailer Hire Agreement."}, {"p": "“Company” shall mean Tanker Rent UK Limited, incorporated and registered in England and Wales with company number 04432719 whose registered office is at Grovebury Road, Leighton Buzzard, Bedfordshire, LU7 4TS."}, {"p": "“Contract” shall mean the contract between the Company and the Hirer for the letting out of a Trailer on hire by the Company to the Hirer in accordance with this Master Hire Agreement and a Trailer Hire Agreement involving an individual Trailer."}, {"p": "“Deposit” shall mean (where applicable) the amount specified as such in the Trailer Hire Agreement."}, {"p": "“Extended Hire Period” shall be as defined in clause 1.3.2."}, {"p": "“Hire Period” shall mean in respect of any Trailer the hire period stated in the Trailer Hire Agreement relating to such Trailer."}, {"p": "“Hirer” shall mean the person or firm who takes a Trailer on hire from the Company, as specified in the Trailer Hire Agreement."}, {"p": "“Master Hire Agreement” shall mean the terms and conditions set out in this document as amended from time to time in accordance with clause 19."}, {"p": "“Parties” shall mean the Company and the Hirer and “Party” shall mean either of them."}, {"p": "“Rental” shall mean in respect of any Trailer the rental stated in the Trailer Hire Agreement relating to such Trailer."}, {"p": "“Risk Period” shall be as defined in clause 2.6."}, {"p": "“Trailer” shall mean any Trailer that is described in and subject to a Trailer Hire Agreement. Any reference to a Trailer includes all ancillary or specialist equipment fitted to any such Trailer including but not limited to that set out in the Trailer Hire Agreement."}, {"p": "“Trailers” shall be interpreted accordingly."}, {"p": "“Trailer Check Out Sheet” shall mean the form provided by the Company and to be signed by the Hirer in accordance with clause 2.4, confirming the condition of the Trailer at the commencement of the Hire Period."}, {"p": "“Trailer Hire Agreement” shall mean an individual agreement for the hiring of a Trailer. Each Trailer Hire Agreement will contain details of the Hire Period and the Rental applicable to the hire of the Trailer by the Company to the Hirer."}, {"h": "1. Hire"}, {"p": "1.1 Should the Hirer wish to take a Trailer on hire from the Company:"}, {"p": "1.1.1 the Hirer shall notify the Company and provide the Company with as much information as the Company reasonably requests in order to prepare a draft Trailer Hire Agreement for the Trailer requested;"}, {"p": "1.1.2 following receipt of the information requested from the Hirer, the Company shall, as soon as reasonably practicable, either: (a) notify the Hirer that it declines to provide the Trailer to the Hirer; or (b) provide the Hirer with a draft Trailer Hire Agreement;"}, {"p": "1.1.3 if the Company provides the Hirer with a draft Trailer Hire Agreement according to clause 1.1.2 (b), the Parties shall discuss and agree that draft Trailer Hire Agreement; and"}, {"p": "1.1.4 once agreed, the Parties shall have the draft Trailer Hire Agreement executed by their respective authorised representatives. Where the Hirer’s representative is other than a director of the Hirer, the Hirer will provide evidence satisfactory to the Company that such representative has been properly authorised."}, {"p": "1.2 Each Trailer Hire Agreement shall form a separate Contract between the Parties, upon and subject to the terms and conditions of this Master Hire Agreement. A Contract shall be deemed to be made upon and be effective from the date upon which the Trailer Hire Agreement is executed on behalf of both Parties."}, {"p": "1.3 The Company shall hire the Trailer to the Hirer for the Hire Period, which shall commence in accordance with clause 2.1 and shall continue, unless otherwise terminated in accordance with this Master Hire Agreement, until the expiry of the Hire Period, at which point:"}, {"p": "1.3.1 the Contract shall automatically expire, and the Hirer shall return the Trailer to the Company in accordance with the provisions of clause 10.4 below; or"}, {"p": "1.3.2 the Hirer shall have the right to extend the Hire Period for an additional month by retaining the Trailer at the end of such Hire Period, subject to availability and provided that:"}, {"p": "(a) the Hirer is not then in breach of any of its obligations pursuant to the Contract applicable to the Trailer;"}, {"p": "(b) the Hirer gives the Company written notice of its intention to extend the Hire Period no later than fourteen (14) days prior to the end of the initial Hire Period or any extended Hire Period (as applicable);"}, {"p": "(c) the Hirer continues to pay Rental to the Company at the rate specified in the Trailer Hire Agreement;"}, {"p": "(d) the Company has not given notice to terminate the Contract."}, {"p": "(e) the Hirer may not extend Hire Period beyond a period of twelve (12) months from the date of the commencement of the Hire Period without the prior written consent of the Company."}, {"p": "1.4 Without prejudice to any other rights it may have, the Company has the right to terminate the Contract at any time by giving the Hirer not less than one month's prior written notice, such termination to take effect no earlier than the end of the initial Hire Period as stated in the Trailer Hire Agreement."}, {"p": "1.5 If at the end of the Hire Period (or the Extended Hire Period according to clause 1.3.2 above) the Company has not received notice from the Hirer that it wishes to extend the Hire Period by a further month in accordance with clause 1.3.2, the Hire Period will be deemed to have expired at the end of the last month in respect of which Rental was duly paid, unless the Company agrees to the contrary in writing."}, {"p": "1.6 During the Hire Period and for the purposes of the Road Traffic Regulation Act 1984, the Hirer shall be liable to the Company in respect of any offences which may be committed in respect of a Trailer when stationary and when a fixed penalty notice is issued including but not limited to:"}, {"p": "1.6.1 being on a road during the hours of darkness without the lights or reflectors required by law;"}, {"p": "1.6.2 waiting, or being left or parked, or being loaded or unloaded in a road;"}, {"p": "1.6.3 being used or kept on a public road without the Trailer test certificates being exhibited on the Trailer in the prescribed manner;"}, {"p": "1.6.4 the non-payment of the charge made at a street parking place and any excess charge which may be incurred in pursuance of an order under section 107 and 108 of the Road Traffic Regulation Act 1984."}, {"p": "1.7 The Company shall not, other than in the exercise of its rights under this Master Hire Agreement or applicable law, interfere with the Hirer’s quiet possession of the Trailer."}, {"h": "2. Commencement of Hire and Risk"}, {"p": "2.1 The Hire Period will commence when an authorised representative of the Hirer collects the Trailer from the Company on the Collection Date."}, {"p": "2.2 The Hirer shall use all reasonable endeavours to collect the Trailer by the Collection Date. If the Hirer does not collect the Trailer from the Company on the Collection Date, then:"}, {"p": "2.2.1 the Parties may agree another Collection Date in accordance with clause 19; or"}, {"p": "2.2.2 if the Hirer has not contacted the Company within forty eight (48) hours of the Collection Date to arrange a new Collection Date, the Rentals will start accruing from the Collection Date and the Company may terminate the Contract on written notice to the Hirer and the Company shall refund to the Hirer any advance Rental paid in respect of the Trailer."}, {"p": "2.3 In the absence of any other agreement between the Parties in writing, collection of the Trailer shall take place during the Company’s normal business hours and at the premises nominated by the Company."}, {"p": "2.4 When collecting any Trailer from the Company, the Hirer shall have its representative sign the relevant Trailer Check Out Sheet for the Trailer. In any event, the physical collection of the Trailer or the signing of the Trailer Check Out Sheet by the Hirer’s representative (in both instances"}, {"p": "“Collection”) shall constitute conclusive evidence that the Hirer has examined the Trailer and has found it to be in good condition, complete and fit in every way for the purpose for which it is intended."}, {"p": "2.5 The Trailer shall at all times remain the property of the Company, and the Hirer shall have no right, title or interest in or to the Trailer (save the right to possession and use of the Trailer subject to the terms and conditions of this Master Hire Agreement)."}, {"p": "2.6 Risk in any Trailer (including but not limited to any risk of any damage to or loss or destruction or theft of that Trailer or of any loss or damage caused by the Trailer) shall pass to the Hirer on the Hirer’s Collection of the Trailer concerned. The Trailer shall remain at the sole risk of the Hirer during the Hire Period, the Extended Hire Period and any other further term during which the Trailer is in the possession, custody or control of the Hirer (“Risk Period”) until such time as the Trailer is redelivered to the Company."}, {"h": "3. Rental"}, {"p": "3.1 The Hirer will pay to the Company monthly in advance (unless otherwise specified in the Trailer Hire Agreement) the Rental stated in the Trailer Hire Agreement (together with VAT and any other applicable taxes and duties or similar charges which shall be payable by the Hirer at the rate and in the manner from time to time prescribed by law according to the terms of clause 12 below), the first such payment to be made on the date of execution of the Trailer Hire Agreement by the Parties and subsequent payments to be made by standing order on the first day of each month of the Hire Period (unless otherwise specified in the Trailer Hire Agreement) without prior demand by the Company."}, {"p": "3.2 The Deposit is a deposit against default by the Hirer of payment of any Rental or any loss of or damage caused to the Trailer according to the terms in clauses 7.5, 10.3 and 10.4.4 below. Where a Trailer Hire Agreement specifies that a Deposit is payable in respect of a Contract, the Hirer shall, prior to the commencement of the Hire Period, pay the Deposit to the Company. If the Hirer fails to pay any Rental in accordance with the Contract or causes any loss or damage to the Trailer (in whole or in part), the Company shall be entitled to apply the Deposit against such default, loss or damage. The Hirer shall pay to the Company any sums deducted from the Deposit within 10 business days of a demand for the same. The Deposit (or any remaining balance of the Deposit) shall be refundable within five business days of the end of the Hire Period."}, {"p": "3.3 All payments due under the Coniract (if not made by standing order) shall be made to the Company at its address specified in this Master Hire Agreement or at such other address as the Company may from time to time communicate to the Hirer. Any payments sent by post shall be so sent at the risk of the Hirer. 3.4 Time for payment of each and every sum due from the Hirer under the Contract shall be of the essence."}, {"p": "3.5 All amounts due under the Contract shall be paid in full without any set-off, counterclaim, deduction or withholding (other than any deduction or withholding of tax as required by law)."}, {"h": "4. Use of Trailers"}, {"p": "4.1 The Hirer shall keep and operate the Trailer in a suitable environment and use the Trailer for the purpose of its business only and in accordance with any operating instructions, including but not limited to any weight tolerances of the Trailer. The Trailer is not to be used, and the Hirer will not permit them to be used, for any purposes for which they are not expressly designed. Further the Hirer will not use or permit the Trailer to be used for driving tuition, racing, or pace making, or for competing in any rally or any other form of motor sport, or for any unlawful purpose whatsoever."}, {"p": "4.2 The Hirer agrees that it will not:"}, {"p": "4.2.1 without prior written consent of the Company effect any mechanical or other modification of any sort to the Trailer, make any alterations or additions or removals, fit any towing equipment or other accessories or non-standard tyres, and any such additions, alterations or modified parts which may be made (whether with or without consent) shall become part of the Trailer and shall belong to the owner of the Trailer."}, {"p": "4.2.2 remove or interfere with any identification marks or plates affixed to the Trailer nor attempt or purport to do so nor permit the same, in order to ensure that the Trailer remains identifiable as the Company’s property."}, {"p": "4.2.3 deface in any way the paintwork or bodywork of the Trailer."}, {"p": "4.3 The Hirer relies on its own skill and judgment in selecting the Trailer and hereby warrants that it has not made known to the Company any special purpose for which the Trailer is required."}, {"h": "5. Duties of the Hirer"}, {"p": "5.1 The Hirer shall during the continuance of the Contract (and thereafter in accordance with clauses 10.6 and 11 below):"}, {"p": "5.1.1 pay to the Company interest at the rate of 4% per annum above the base rate of Nat West PLC (or its successor) in force from time to time on all overdue sums, such interest accruing on a daily basis from the due date until actual payment, whether before or after judgment;"}, {"p": "5.1.2 ensure that the Trailer is operated properly and safely and without risk to health by drivers who at all times hold valid and current driving licenses in the appropriate classes and be responsible for the proper training of all such drivers in relation to all relevant matters; 5.1.3 at the Hirer’s own cost, maintain and service the Trailer strictly in accordance with the recommendations of the Trailer manufacturer in relation to those matters, and the Hirer shall also maintain, repair and service any ancillary and/or specialist equipment which may be attached to or incorporated into any Trailer strictly in accordance with the recommendations of the manufacturer(s) of any such equipment. In any event, the Hirer shall be responsible for the cost of properly maintaining, servicing and repairing any additions or accessories to the Trailer which may be added by or on behalf of the Hirer after the commencement of the Hire Period and regardless of whether the Company has consented to the same; 5.1.4 in all cases, pay for all fuel and lubricants for the proper running of the Trailer and insure that sufficient antifreeze of the recommended type is at all relevant times maintained in the relevant ancillary equipment;"}, {"p": "5.1.5 indemnify the Company on demand against all fines, penalties and liabilities imposed on the Company or arising in respect of any non-compliance or contravention of any transport, traffic or other law or regulation in respect of the Trailer, together with any cost or expense relating thereto incurred by the Company;"}, {"p": "5.1.6 not take or allow any Trailer to be taken out of the United Kingdom mainland without receiving the prior written consent of the Company and, in the event of that consent being given, only on such terms as the Company deems it fit;"}, {"p": "5.1.7 subject to clauses 8.5, 8.6 and 8.7 indemnify the Company in full against all liabilities, claims, costs, expenses, damages and losses suffered or incurred by the Company in respect of any loss of or damage to the Trailer arising as a result of or in connection with the negligence, recklessness or improper use, mishandling or operation of the Trailer or resulting from any accident or incident in which any Trailer may be involved or from any other circumstances;"}, {"p": "5.1.8 not sell, assign, sublease, lend, or otherwise dispose of or part with (or offer to do the same) possession of any Trailer or its part or assign or charge the benefit of the Contract nor attempt or purport to do so nor create or permit the creation of any lien or other security interest on the Trailer;"}, {"p": "5.1.9 not suffer or permit the Trailer to be confiscated, seized or taken out of its possession or control, but if the Trailer is so confiscated, seized or taken, the Hirer shall notify the Company and the Hirer shall at its own expense use best endeavours to retain and recover possession and control of any Trailer of which the Hirer loses possession or control;"}, {"p": "5.1.10 permit or procure permission for the Company or its authorised representatives at all reasonable times to enter upon the premises where the Trailer and/or the records referred to in clause 5.1.12 (d) below may from time to time be garaged or parked or kept to inspect and test the condition of the Trailer and/or to inspect such records;"}, {"p": "5.1.11 notify the Company of any change in the Hirer’s address, keep the Trailer in the possession or control of the Hirer and, upon request by the Company, promptly inform the Company of the whereabouts of the Trailer;"}, {"p": "5.1.12 in respect of the condition and the maintenance of the Trailer, and without prejudice to the generality of clause 5.1.3, be solely responsible at its own cost for all manufacturer recommended periodic operator/driver checks and also for the following in relation to the Trailer:"}, {"p": "(a) regularly checking and adjusting as necessary the radiator, battery and engine fiuid and all other reservoir levels;"}, {"p": "(b) regularly cleaning the exterior and interior of the Trailer;"}, {"p": "(c) promptly repairing all damage (save for any repairs which are the responsibility of the Company according to clause 6.1 below);"}, {"p": "(d) keeping full and accurate record of all operating, maintenance and repair services carried out in relation to each Trailer and in relation to any ancillary or specialist equipment fitted to or incorporated into any Trailer;"}, {"p": "(e) arranging, at the direction of the Company, for the regular servicing of the Trailer by parties nominated by the Company and delivering the Trailer to and collecting the Trailer from such parties."}, {"p": "5.1.13 arrange for the Trailer to be tested and obtain a new Trailer test certificate or renew the same before expiry as required by any relevant legislation;"}, {"p": "5.1.14 not use or permit the Trailer to be used or operated in a manner contrary to any statutory provision or regulation or in any way contrary to law, including but not limited to the regulations affecting:"}, {"p": "(a) the suitability of the Trailer to be used to transport the substance(s) the Hirer intends to use the Trailer to transport;"}, {"p": "(b) maintenance and usage of tyres and/or specialist equipment; and"}, {"p": "(c) the carriage of hazardous or dangerous substances."}, {"p": "5.1.15 not, in the opinion of the Company, not do or permit to be done any act or thing which will or may jeopardise the right, title or interest of the Company in the Trailer, jeopardise the Trailer or permit it to be placed in jeopardy including without limitation to keep the Trailer free of any distraint or distress, execution or other legal process;"}, {"p": "5.1.16 keep the Company fully informed of all material matters relating to the Trailer."}, {"h": "6. Maintenance and Repair"}, {"p": "6.1 During the Risk Period, the Hirer shall (uniess otherwise specified in the Trailer Hire Agreement) at its expense have the Trailer (including any ancillary or specialist equipment which may at the date of delivery to the Hirer be attached to or incorporated into the vehicles) serviced and maintained in good and substantial repair in order to keep it in as good an operating condition as it was on the Collection Date (fair wear and tear only excluded), with such maintenance including, but not limited to:"}, {"p": "6.1.1 the replacement of worn, damaged and lost parts;"}, {"p": "6.1.2 the replacement or repair of tyres other than strictly in accordance with the Company's tyre policy (or at the election of the Company the tyre policy of the party from which the Company has the Trailer on hire) as published by the Company (or by such party as the case may be) from time to time;"}, {"p": "6.1.3 any work of service, maintenance or repair due to be performed or otherwise required at any time whilst the Trailer is out of the United Kingdom (regardless of whether the Company shall have consented to the Trailer being so removed from the United Kingdom);"}, {"p": "6.1.4 the service, maintenance and repair of any additional or modified item which may be attached to or incorporated into the Trailer or modified after the Collection Date, regardless of whether the Company shall have consented to such addition or modification."}, {"p": "6.2 The Hirer shall make good any damage to the Trailer, including but not limited to:"}, {"p": "6.2.1 any damage resulting directly or indirectly from any accident or incident involving the Trailer or from the goods or load carried by any Trailer or any damage deliberately, negligently or recklessly caused to the Trailer (including but not limited to driver abuse);"}, {"p": "6.2.2 any damage or want of repair resulting directly or indirectly from any breach by the Hirer of its obligations under this Master Hire Agreement or any Trailer Hire Agreement;"}, {"p": "6.2.3 any damage to running gear, springs, tanker equipment, airbags, tyres, mudwings, siderails, landing legs, manway access ladders, the internal condition of the barrel and/or exterior cladding; and"}, {"p": "6.2.4 any other form of damage which is expressed in this Master Hire Agreement or any Trailer Hire Agreement to be an obligation of the Hirer."}, {"p": "6.3 Without prejudice to the foregoing, the Company shall at its discretion and for such period or periods as the Company shall deem necessary, be entitled to replace any Trailer with a Trailer of the same or similar type to which the terms of the Contract shall apply."}, {"p": "6.4 Where it is specified in a Trailer Hire Agreement that the Company shall provide a chassis maintenance service in relation to the Trailer, then this shall consist of and be limited to:"}, {"p": "6.4.1 normal servicing by way of programmed maintenance of the chassis of the Trailer (excluding topping up fluids on ancillary equipment between services) as set out in the chassis manufacturer's applicable programmed maintenance schedules;"}, {"p": "6.4.2 carrying out timed safety inspections as required by the Department of Transport for the Hirer's operator's license purposes and Department of Transport testing as applicable to the Trailer, provided that should the required frequency or cost of such inspections or testing result in an additional cost to the Company, such additional cost shall be reflected in increased Rental from the date such additional cost was incurred and the Hirer shall pay such increased Rental accordingly;"}, {"p": "6.4.3 carrying out such safety inspections in accordance with the Hirer's operator's license requirements, unless otherwise agreed with the Hirer. In addition, the Company shall be responsible on behalf of the Hirer for keeping safety inspection reports and programmed maintenance records in relation to the chassis and will produce them as soon as practicable for Department of Transport examiners or make them available for inspection by the Hirer;"}, {"p": "6.4.4 to the extent deemed necessary by the Company, providing replacement batteries for the ancillary equipment concerned;"}, {"p": "6.4.5 carrying out any of the following to the extent deemed necessary by the Company: repairs to and replacement of mechanical, hydraulic, electrical and/or electronic equipment or systems fitted to or incorporated within the chassis of the Trailer at the Collection Date; and"}, {"p": "6.4.6 a UK 24 hour breakdown/roadside attendance in relation to the chassis of the Trailer."}, {"p": "6.5 Where it is specified in a Trailer Hire Agreement that the Company shall provide a repair service in relation to the Trailer, then this shall consist of and be limited to the replacement or repair of tyres necessitated by normal wear and tear subject to clause 6.1.2 but excluding any replacement or repair necessitated by accidental or deliberate damage howsoever caused."}, {"p": "6.6 Where it is specified in a Trailer Hire Agreement that the Company shall provide a maintenance and repair service in relation to ancillary or specialised equipment of the Trailer, then this shall consist of and be limited to:"}, {"p": "6.6.1 normal servicing by way of programmed maintenance of the body/or the ancillary equipment of the Trailer, as the case may be (excluding topping up fluids between services) and as set out in the relevant manufacturer's applicable programmed maintenance schedules;"}, {"p": "6.6.2 keeping any relevant safety inspection reports and programmed maintenance records (for the body/and or ancillary equipment as the case may be) and producing them as soon as practicable for Department of Transport examiners or for the inspection by the Hirer and"}, {"p": "6.6.3 carrying out any of the following to the extent deemed necessary by the Company: repairs to and replacement of mechanical, hydraulic, electrical and electronic equipment or systems fitted to, part of, or incorporated within the body and/or the ancillary equipment as the case may be of the Trailer as at the Collection Date."}, {"h": "7. Insurance"}, {"p": "71 The Hirer shall, at its own expense, throughout the Hire Period and the Risk Period, obtain and keep the following insurances with an insurance company of good repute in respect of the Trailer:"}, {"p": "7.1.1 insurance of the Trailer to a value not less than its full replacement value (as specified in the Trailer Hire Agreement) with comprehensive cover against loss or damage from all risks."}, {"p": "7.1.2 insurance for such amounts as a prudent owner or operaior of the Trailer would insure for, or such amount as the Company may from time to time reasonably require, to cover any third party or public liability risks of whatever nature and however arising in connection with the Trailer; and 7.1.3 insurance against such other or further risks relating to the Trailer as may be required by law, together with such other insurance as the Company may from time to time consider reasonably necessary and advise to the Hirer."}, {"p": "7.2 The Hirer shall:"}, {"p": "7.2.1 notify its insurers that the Trailer is on hire from the Company and request the insurers to endorse a note of such interest on the policy of insurance naming the Company as loss payee;"}, {"p": "7.2.2 on demand, show to the Company the policy of insurance, the premium receipts and insurance certificate; and"}, {"p": "7.2.3 not use or allow the Trailer to be used for any purpose not permitted by the terms and conditions of the policy of insurance or allow to be done any act or thing whereby the insurance may be invalidated."}, {"p": "7.3 Ifthe Hirer shall default in the payment of any premiums in respect of the insurance, the Company may pay such premium, in which event the Hirer shall repay the premium amount to the Company on demand. The Hirer shall indemnify the Company against all loss or damage to the Trailer or caused by the Trailer not recoverable by the Company under the policy of insurance."}, {"p": "7.4 Where an event or accident shall occur which is a risk covered by the Hirer’s insurance under this Master Hire Agreement, the Hirer shall immediately notify the Company of the event or accident. The Hirer shall not settle any claim without the consent of the Company, shall allow the Company to take over the conduct of negotiations (except in relation to the Hirer's own claims for loss and damages) and shall at the expense of the Hirer take such proceedings (in the sole name of the Hirer or at the direction of the Company jointly with the Company) as the parties shall agree. The Company shall hold all sums so recovered, on trust for the parties and shall pay or apply the same according to the terms of the settlement, or the court’s ruling or judgement and as _ provided in this Master Hire Agreement . If any Trailer is declared as a total loss, the hire of the affected Trailer shall terminate. In such event the Company shall apply any proceeds of insurance received by it at its option:"}, {"p": "7.4.1 towards an immediate replacement of equivalent value, which replacement shall be deemed to be included in the applicable Trailer Hire Agreement for all purposes and the Hirer shall continue to be liable to pay Rental as if such loss had not taken place: or"}, {"p": "7.4.2 in or towards payment to the Company of the sum necessary to compensate the Company for all its reasonable and direct losses including but not limited to the loss of profit suffered as a result of the loss of that Trailer."}, {"p": "7.5 The Company shall have the right (always at the cost of the Hirer) itself to repair or have repaired any Trailer which is the subject of an accident or event resulting in damage to the Trailer. Any such costs incurred by the Company (including parts and labour) shall be a debt payable to the Company by the Hirer on demand and such costs may be partly or wholly recovered from any Deposit. If the Company does not choose to do so the Hirer shall be liable to reinstate or repair at its own expense any Trailer which has not become a total loss and in any event shall continue to pay Rental in respect of such Trailer during such reinstatement or repair."}, {"p": "7.6 The Hirer will be liable to pay the Company any amount deducted by the insurers by way of excess or in respect of damage caused to the Trailer prior to the date of total loss."}, {"h": "8. General Liability"}, {"p": "8.1 Subject to clauses 8.5, 8.6 and 8.7, the Hirer shall be solely responsible for and hold the Company fully indemnified against all claims, liabilities, losses, damages,, costs and expenses which may be brought against or incurred by the Company as a direct result of any accident or incident involving the Trailer (save to the extent that the same arise direcily as a result of any breach by the Company of its obligations pursuant to the Contract)."}, {"p": "8.2 The Company warrants that, as at the Collection Date, the Trailer will substantially conform to its specification (as made available by the Company), be of satisfactory quality (subject to its condition as set out in the Trailer Check Out Form) and fit for any purpose held out by the Company."}, {"p": "8.3 Subject to clause 8.2, the Company does not hire out the Trailer subject to any other condition or warranty express, implied or statutory in connection with the quality, performance or the fitness for any purpose or age of the Trailer and any such conditions and warranties are hereby expressly excluded insofar as permitted by statute and the Company will not be responsible for any liability, claim, loss, damage or expense of any kind or nature caused directly or indirectly by the Trailer or their use (save to the extent that the same arise directly as a result of any breach by the Company of its obligations pursuant to the Contract)."}, {"p": "8.4 Subject to clauses 8.6 and 876, the Company's total aggregate liability to the Hirer arising under or in connection with the Contract, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), misrepresentation, restitution or otherwise, shall not exceed 100% of the Rental paid or payable by the Hirer."}, {"p": "8.5 Subject to clauses 8.6 and 8.7, the Hirer's total aggregate liability to the Company arising under or in connection with the Contract, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), misrepresentation, restitution or otherwise, shall not exceed four hundred thousand pounds (£400,000) in aggregate for the Hire Period."}, {"p": "8.6 In no circumstances shall either Party be liable for any indirect or consequential losses suffered by the other, including but not limited to indirect loss of contracts and loss of anticipated profits, loss of sales or business, loss of anticipated savings, loss of use or corruption of software, data or information and loss of or damage to goodwill."}, {"p": "8.7 Nothing in the Contract shall exclude or restrict or shall be interpreted or construed as in any way excluding or restricting the liability of either Party for death or personal injury caused by the negligence of such Party, its employees or agents."}, {"h": "9. Ownership"}, {"p": "9.1 As between the Parties, and in accordance with clause 2.5 above, the Trailer shall at all times remain the property of the Company and the Hirer shall have no rights to the Trailer other than as Hirer under the Contract and the Hirer shall not do or permit or cause to be done any matter or thing whereby the rights of the Company or any such third party in respect of the Trailer are or may be prejudicially affected."}, {"h": "10. Termination"}, {"p": "10.1 If the Hirer shall:"}, {"p": "10.1.1 fail to pay any Rental or other sum payable under the Contract and remains in default not less than 14 days after being notified in writing to make such payment or shall commit a material breach of any of the other terms and conditions (whether express or implied) of the Contract and fail to remedy such material breach within 30 days of being requested in writing to do so by the Company;"}, {"p": "10.1.2 repeatedly breach any of the terms of the Contract in such a manner as to reasonably justify the opinion that its conduct is inconsistent with it having the intention or ability to give effect to the terms of the Contract; or"}, {"p": "10.1.3 do or allow to be done any act or thing which in the opinion of the Company may jeopardize the Company’s rights in the Trailer or any part of it, then in each and every such case the Hirer shall be deemed to have repudiated the Contract and the Company may immediately by notice in writing to the Hirer terminate the Contract and any other Contracts between the Parties."}, {"p": "10.2 If any of the following events shall occur, namely:"}, {"p": "10.2.1 if any distress, execution, or other legal process shall be levied on or against any of the Trailer or any part of it or against any premises where the same may be or against any of the Hirer’s goods or other property; or"}, {"p": "10.2.2 if the Hirer shall:"}, {"p": "(a) enter into any liquidation;"}, {"p": "(b) call any meeting of its creditors with a view to rescheduling any of its debts, or make a proposal for or enter into any compromise or arrangement with its creditors;"}, {"p": "(c) have a receiver or administrative receiver appointed over all or any of its undertakings or assets or have an application made to court to the same effect;"}, {"p": "(d) experience the appointment or the presentation of a petition for the appointment of an administrator under the provisions on Part II of the Insolvency Act 1986;"}, {"p": "(e) suspend, or threaten to suspend, payment of its debts or be unable to pay its debts as they fall due or admit inability to pay its debts or be deemed by virtue of section 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986 to be unable to pay its debts:"}, {"p": "(f) have a petition filed, a notice given, a resolution passed, or an order made, for or in connection with its winding up;"}, {"p": "(g) apply to court for, or obtain, a moratorium under Part A1 of the Insolvency Act 1986;"}, {"p": "(h) being an individual, have a bankruptcy petition presented against him or her or be the subject of a bankruptcy order or an interim order under the Insolvency Act 1986;"}, {"p": "(i) have a creditor or encumbrancer attach or take possession of the whole or any part of its assets;"}, {"p": "(j) have a distress, execution, sequestration or other such process levied or enforced on or sued against the whole or any part of its assets;"}, {"p": "(k) experience any event or have proceedings taken against it in any jurisdiction to which it is subject that has an effect equivalent or similar to any of the events mentioned in clauses 10.2.2(a) —(j) (inclusive); (I) have its financial position deteriorate so far as to reasonably justify the opinion that its ability to give effect to the terms of the Contract is in jeopardy; or"}, {"p": "(n) suspend or cease, or threaten to suspend or cease, carrying on all or a substantial part of its business, then in each and every such case above the Company may, on written notice to the Hirer, terminate the Contract and no payments subsequently accepted by the Company without knowledge of such termination shall in any way prejudice or affect the operation of this clause."}, {"p": "10.3 In addition to any other sums expressed to be payable according to the terms of the Contract, the Hirer shall upon the expiry or termination of the Contract, upon demand pay to the Company (and the Company may partly or wholly recover such sums from any Deposit):"}, {"p": "10.3.1 all arrears of Rental then due and all other sums accrued due and unpaid at the date of termination, together with interest thereon payable under clause 5.1.1 of this Master Hire Agreement ; and"}, {"p": "10.3.2 where the Contract is terminated in accordance with clauses 10.1 or 10.2, a sum equal to the whole of the Rental that would (but for the termination) have been payable if the Contract had continued from the date of such demand to the end of the Hire Period."}, {"p": "10.3.3 the cost of all repairs and/or other work required in order to bring the Trailer up to the standard required in order for them to comply with clause 10.4 below; and"}, {"p": "10.3.4 any other sums which are or become due to the Company or to which the Company is entitled by way of damages together with but not limited to sums payable by the Hirer according to clause 10.4.3 below."}, {"p": "10.4 On termination of the hire of any Trailer howsoever or whenever occasioned or on expiry of the Hire Period:"}, {"p": "10.4.1 the Hirer shall no longer be in possession of the Trailer with the Company's consent and shall immediately without delay (and in any event within 24 hours of the expiry or termination of the Contract) return the Trailer (including each Trailer’s fully completed service records (including but not limited to a wash out certificate) or a certified true copy together with accessories/specialist equipment where fitted)) to the Company at such address as the Company may direct in good order and in good working condition and at the Hirer’s expense and risk."}, {"p": "10.4.2 whenever a Trailer is retured by the Hirer to the Company or repossessed by the Company then it shall be in a condition commensurate with its age and mileage but will in any event comply with the following standards:"}, {"p": "(a) be free from accidental or deliberate damage, and with a clean interior;"}, {"p": "(b) be in the original colour, have any paint damage made good and any Hirer branding removed and where this is not possible, the Company shall be entitled to remove the Hirer branding at the Hirer’s expense;"}, {"p": "(c) be free from any mechanical, electrical, electronic, pneumatic or hydraulic defects;"}, {"p": "(d) have batteries in such a condition as to enable the ancillary equipment engine, if any, to be started from cold;"}, {"p": "(e) in respect of the tyres:"}, {"p": "(i) have the statutory minimum legal requirement of tread from time to time on each tyre of uncut rubber with no lumps or bulges nor any surface cuts in excess of 25mm long;"}, {"p": "(ii) have no cross-maiching of tyres on the same axle; and"}, {"p": "(f) the tyre make to be the same as originally specified by the Trailer manufacturer as either standard or optional factory fitted equipment; have all original bodywork and manufacturer approved and fitted equipment (or replacements) intact;"}, {"p": "(g) be complete with tools (or replacements) and otherwise as originally equipped;"}, {"p": "(h) be in such a condition as would allow it to pass the test required to obtain a department of transport test certificate;"}, {"p": "(i) be in a condition commensurate with the Hirer having duly performed all of its obligations under the Contract; 10.4.3 should the Hirer not return the Trailer to the Company in accordance with clause 10.4.1, then without prejudice to any of its other rights under this Master Hire Agreement, the Company or its authorised representatives may, at any time after such termination/expiry of the Hire Period and without notice, retake possession of the Trailer and for such purpose enter upon any premises (a) belonging to or in the occupation or control of the Hirer or (b) where the Trailer is located. The Hirer shall be responsible for all costs, charges and expenses so incurred in the Company's retaking possession of the Trailer as aforesaid. The Hirer shall also bear the reasonable costs incurred by the Company at any time in ascertaining the whereabouts of the Trailer and/ or the Hirer. Any such costs, charges or expenses so incurred by the Company shall be a debt payable to the Company by the Hirer on demand and the Company may partly or wholly recover such sums from any Deposit;"}, {"p": "10.4.4 following the return or repossession of any Trailer to or by the Company (as applicable), the Company or its appointed agent shall within a reasonable period:"}, {"p": "(a) inspect the Trailer to ascertain its condition. In the event that any such Trailer does not comply with the standards set out in clause 10.4.2 the Company shall be entitled to carry out or have carried out such work to the Trailer so as to reasonably resiore it to that condition and the cost of such work (including parts and labour) shall be a debt payable to the Company by the Hirer on demand and the Company may partly or wholly recover such sums from any Deposit; and"}, {"p": "(b) inspect the Trailer’s fully completed service records where it has access to the same. In any case, where either:"}, {"p": "(i) the Hirer does not provide the Company with the Trailer’s fully completed inspection and service records (as referred to in sub clause 5.1.12 (d) above) on the return of the Trailer or within 2 working days of the repossession of the Trailer; or (ii) such service records do not demonstrate full compliance by the Hirer with the provisions of clause 5.1 above and/or the Contract generally, then without prejudice to its other rights hereunder the Company shall be entitled to have carried out upon the Trailer and upon any relevant ancillary or specialist equipment a major service or equivalent (as defined from time to time by the manufacturer of the Trailer or of such ancillary or specialist equipment) and such other work as may be appropriate for it to be capable of being sold as a Trailer which has been maintained, serviced, repaired and otherwise operated in accordance with the standards referred to in clauses 4.1 and 5.1 above. The cost of such work (including parts and labor) shall be a debt payable to the Company by the Hirer on demand and the Company may partly or wholly recover such sums from any Deposit;"}, {"p": "10.4.5 should any monies be due to the Company according to the provisions of clauses 10.4.3 or 10.4.4 above, then without prejudice to its other rights the Company is hereby permitted to raise an invoice between the Hirer and the Company in order to affect payment of any or all such amounts due. 10.5 Any termination of the Contract shall not affect the coming into force or continuance in force of any provision of the Contract which is expressly or by implication intended to come into force or continue in force on or after termination including but not limited to clauses/, 8, 9, 10, 11 and 12. 10.6 The expiry or termination of the Contract shall not affect any rights of the Company or liabilities of the Hirer subsisting at the date of termination."}, {"h": "11. Continuation of Payment"}, {"p": "11.1 Without prejudice to the provisions of clause 10 of this Master Hire Agreement and the rights of the Company, as from the expiry or termination of the Contract and until such time as the Trailer is returned to the possession of the Company, the Hirer will:"}, {"p": "11.1.1 pay the Company a daily sum (payable in arrears) for the continued use of the Trailer for each such day the Trailer is not so returned at a pro rata daily rate equivalent to the Rental previously due in respect thereof; and"}, {"p": "11.1.2 continue to have, with regard to the Trailer, all of the obligations which it had during the continuance of the Hire Period."}, {"p": "11.2 This clause 11 shall not confer upon the Hirer any right to the continued use or possession of the Trailer."}, {"h": "12. Value Added Tax"}, {"p": "12.1 The Rental set out in the Trailer Hire Agreement is shown exclusive of value added tax and the Hirer shall, in addition, pay to the Company value added tax or any similar tax or duty on the Rental calculated at the prevailing rate from time to time in force. Where the Hirer is required to pay the Company any other sums according to the Contract then the value added tax shall, where applicable, be payable on those sums at the prevailing rate from time to time."}, {"h": "13. Company’s Intervention"}, {"p": "13.1 If the Hirer fails to comply with or commits a breach of any provision of the Contract, the Company may, at its discretion and without prejudice to the right of the Company (where applicable) to treat that non-compliance as an event entitling it to terminate the Contract under clause 10 of this Master Hire Agreement, effect compliance on behalf of the Hirer whereupon the Hirer will become liable to pay immediately to the Company any sums expended by the Company together with all costs and expenses including legal costs in connection therewith."}, {"h": "14. Forbearance"}, {"p": "14.1 A delay or failure to exercise, or the single or partial exercise of, any right or remedy on the part of the Company in respect of any of the provisions of the Contract shall in any way waive, restrict or prejudice the further exercise of that or any other right or remedy of the Company under the Contract or operate as or be deemed to be a waiver of any breach by the Hirer of the terms and conditions of the Contract."}, {"h": "15. Notices"}, {"p": "15.1 Any notices given in connection with the Contract must be in writing and may be given to either Party at its registered office (or such other address as it may notify to the other Party to the Contract for such purpose) and will be effectively served:"}, {"p": "15.1.1 on the day of receipt, where any hand delivered letter or email is received on any business day before or during normal working hours; or"}, {"p": "15.1.2 on the following business day, where any hand delivered letter, or email is received either on any business day after normal working hours or on any day which is not a business day; or"}, {"p": "15.1.3 on the second business day following the day of posting, upon dispatch from within the United Kingdom of any posted letter by post office in land first class mail postage pre paid."}, {"p": "15.2 For the purposes of clause 15.1, a business day is any day from Monday to Friday (inclusive) other than United Kingdom bank holidays and normal working hours are between 9.00am and 5.00pm each business day."}, {"h": "16. Set Off"}, {"p": "16.1 The Hirer shall not have any rights of set off against any payment of the Rental or any other payment due under the Contract."}, {"h": "17. Representations"}, {"p": "17.1 The Hirer acknowledges that in entering into the Contract it has not relied upon any advice or representation whether by the Company or any associated company of the Company or any employee or agent of any of the same as to the suitability of any particular Trailer or the suitability and/ or efficacy of any particular method or combination of methods of acquiring the use and/or ownership of Trailer."}, {"h": "18. Headings"}, {"p": "18.1 The headings in this Contract are included for conveyance of reference only and shall not in any way limit or otherwise effect the meaning or interpretation of the Contract."}, {"h": "19. Amendment"}, {"p": "19.1 No amendment to any provision of this Master Hire Agreement or any Trailer Hire Agreement shall be effective or binding on either of the parties unless set forth in writing and executed by a duly authorised representative of each Party."}, {"h": "20. Severability"}, {"p": "20.1 In case any provision in this Master Hire Agreement or any Trailer Hire Agreement shall be invalid, illegal or unenforceable, the validity, legality and enforceability or the remaining provisions shall not in any way be affected or impaired thereby. The invalidity, illegality or unenforceability of any provision in this Master Hire Agreement or any Trailer Hire Agreement in any jurisdiction shall not invalidate or render illegal or unenforceable such provision in any other jurisdiction."}, {"h": "21. Entire Agreement"}, {"p": "21.1 This Master Hire Agreement and any Trailer Hire Agreement made pursuant to this Master Hire Agreement constitutes the entire Contract between the parties with respect to the matters covered in this Master Hire Agreement."}, {"h": "22. No Agency"}, {"p": "22.1 The Hirer is not an agent of the Company and the Hirer shall have no authority to make any representations or enter into any commitments on behalf of the Company or in any way hold itself out as being authorised to act on behalf of the Company."}, {"p": "22.2 Nothing in the Contract is intended to, or shall be deemed to, establish any partnership or joint venture between the Parties, constitute either Party the agent of the other, or authorise either Party to make or enter into any commitments for or on behalf of the other Party."}, {"p": "22.3 Each Party confirms it is acting on its own behalf as a principal in connection with the Contract and not as the agent of any other party."}, {"h": "23. Force Majeure"}, {"p": "23.1 Neither Party shall be liable to the other for any failure or delay in the performance of any of its obligations under the Contract arising directly or indirectly from any act of god, act or consequence of war, enemy action, fire, terrorism, riots, civil commotions, strikes, lock outs, local disturbances, requisition by or under the order of government public or local authority or any other cause beyond the reasonable control of that Party."}, {"p": "23.2 In such circumstances as described in clause 23.1, the time for performance of the affected Party's obligations shall be extended by a period equivalent to the period during which performance of the obligation has been delayed or failed to be performed. If the period of delay or non-performance continues for 4 weeks, the Party not affected may terminate the Contract by giving written notice to the affected Party."}, {"h": "24. Confidential Information"}, {"p": "24.1 Each Party undertakes that it shall not at any time during the Contract, and for a period of 2 years after termination or expiry of the Contract, disclose to any person any information concerning the business, affairs, customers, clients or suppliers of the other Party or of any member of the group of companies to which the other Party belongs, except as permitted by clause 24.2."}, {"p": "24.2 Each Party may disclose the other Party’s confidential information:"}, {"p": "24.2.1 to its employees, officers, representatives or advisers who need to know such information for the purposes of exercising the Party’s rights or carrying out its obligations under or in connection with the Contract. Each Party shall ensure that its employees, officers, representatives or advisers to whom it discloses the other Party’s confidential information comply with clause 24; and"}, {"p": "24.2.2 as may be required by law, a court of competent jurisdiction or any governmental or regulatory authority."}, {"p": "24.3 Neither Party shall use the other Party’s confidential information for any purpose other than to exercise its rights and perform its obligations under or in connection with the Contract."}, {"h": "25. Assignment and Other Dealings"}, {"p": "25.1 This Contract is personal to the Parties and neither Party shall assign, transfer, mortgage, charge, subcontract, delegate, declare a trust over or deal in any other manner with any of its rights and obligations under the Contract without the other Party’s prior written consent (not to be unreasonably withheld or delayed)."}, {"h": "26. Third Party Rights"}, {"p": "26.1 Unless it expressly states otherwise, the Contract does not give rise to any rights under the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 1999 to enforce any term of the Contract. The rights of the Parties to rescind or vary the Contract are not subject to the consent of any other person."}, {"h": "27. Governing Law"}, {"p": "27.1 The Contract and any dispute or claim (including non-contractual disputes or claims) arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or formation shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the law of England and Wales. Each Party irrevocably submits to the exclusive jurisdiction of the English and Welsh courts in settling any dispute or claim (including non-contractual disputes or claims) arising out of or in connection with the Contract or its subject matter or formation."}]};
